          "email": "mvef@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-31 16:17:05.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-19575 tests: retry umount of PCC backend device",
        "message": "LU-19575 tests: retry umount of PCC backend device\n\nsanity-pcc tests intermittently fail in cleanup with \"umount:\n/mnt/pcc.*: target is busy\" (rc 32) even though lsof just\nreported the mount idle. The backend mount might be held briefly\nby references lsof cannot see: the just terminated copytool\nstill releasing its files on exit, or kernel-side PCC mount\nreferences that are dropped asynchronously after detach.\n\numount_loopdev() waits for lsof to report the mount idle but\nattempts the umount only once, so any transient hold fails the\ntest. Retry the umount itself instead. A leaked reference\nstill fails the last attempt.\n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Fable-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-pcc\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I947240f0c72c2aed3d16a42e2e90f36dcb3fd6a9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
